author ai
group map
note The domain crate's map: Map, Path, Step, Anchor and the names and notes they carry, as pure values with no I/O. Map is the only writer: every edit the CLI or the GUI makes is a Map method addressing a path by PathName and a step by StepId, returning Changed (must be used, so a caller cannot drop the fact that the map needs saving) or a count, or a MapError value that the front ends word. Invariants it keeps: path names are unique, and add_path and rename refuse a name that differs from another only in letter case (a name is a file name, and some filesystems ignore case), a step's parent is a step of its path, no step sits under itself, a link names an existing other path, and a linked-to path is not removed. Constructors that take stored values (Path::new, Step::new, Anchor::new) exist for io-map's reader; everything else is made through Map.

